# The source distribution ships the test suite, so it has to ship what the
# suite reads.  Without this file setuptools included `tests/` and left out
# `tools/` and `examples/`, so `python -m unittest discover -s tests` inside an
# unpacked sdist collected 92 of 148 tests and reported two import errors --- a
# suite that looks present and cannot run, which is the failure mode this
# repository exists to argue against.
#
# `measurements/` and the workflow are here for the same reason: they are what
# `tools/check_claims.py` reads when it checks that the README's numbers come
# out of the code.  A claim checker that cannot find the claims is worse than
# no claim checker, because it still exits non-zero for the wrong reason.
include CHANGELOG.md
graft tools
graft examples
graft measurements
recursive-include .github *.yml
global-exclude __pycache__ *.py[cod]
